# JARVIS: Claude + Cursor shared work

Before any task in this repo:

1. Read `plan.md` section 2 "Kaam ke usool" and `docs/CONTRACTS.md` (the canonical contracts; `plan.md` section 4 is a copy), and pick only tasks whose ID starts with `X-` (Cursor lane).
2. Only edit files in the Cursor lane. Lanes (`plan.md` section 2.1; machine-readable copy `.coord/lanes.json`, enforced by the pre-commit hook; `python scripts/coord/check_lane.py --whoowns <path>` prints a path's owner):
   - **Claude:** `src/core/**`, `services/ai_core/**`, `services/utils/**`, `deploy/**`, `scripts/**`, root config (`requirements*.txt`, `pyproject.toml`, `pytest.ini`, `.env*`, `Dockerfile*`, `docker-compose.yml`, `main.py`, `.gitignore`, `.githooks/**`, `.github/**`, `.coord/**`; full list in `.coord/lanes.json`), `CLAUDE.md`, `.cursor/rules/**`, `docs/**`, `README.md`, `tests/core|unit|infrastructure|integration|vision|exhaustive/**`, `tests/conftest.py` and the other `tests/*.py`, and everything on the VPS.
   - **Cursor:** `stonix_ui/**` (frontend + Electron), `services/automation/**`, `services/info/**`, `services/multimedia/**`, `services/system/**`, `assets/**`, `tests/automation/**`, `tests/scripts/**`, `tests/tools/**`, `tests/test_reminders.py`, `tests/test_whatsapp.py`.
   - **Shared:** `plan.md` (only your own task status lines and section 11 "Handoff") and `done_highlight.md` (append-only: add at the end, never edit or remove a line).

   Anything outside the Cursor lane (src/core, services/ai_core, services/utils, deploy, scripts, .env*, requirements, docs, this rule file, VPS) belongs to Claude: write a request in `plan.md` section 11 "Handoff" instead of editing it.
3. Claim a task by changing its status line in `plan.md` to `DOING (cursor, <date time PKT>)`. Mark it `DONE` only after its "Verify" steps pass.
4. After finishing, append an entry at the END of `done_highlight.md` using the template at the top of that file. Never edit, reorder or remove an existing line (the hook rejects it).
5. Never delete or disable a feature, tool, panel or module. The user wants everything working; unsafe things get a guard (confirmation, token, allow-list), not removal.
6. Git: commit only your own files, with `JARVIS_AGENT` set and an explicit pathspec: `git add <your new files>`, then `JARVIS_AGENT=<claude|cursor> git commit -m "[<claude|cursor>] <TASK-ID>: <summary>" -- <your paths>` (PowerShell: `$env:JARVIS_AGENT='cursor'; git commit -m "[cursor] X-NN: <summary>" -- <your paths>`). The pre-commit hook (`scripts/coord/precommit.py`) rejects a missing `JARVIS_AGENT`, paths outside your lane, secret files and values, private terms and removed or changed `done_highlight.md` lines; never bypass it with `--no-verify`. Never `git add -A`, `git stash`, `git reset --hard`, `git checkout <branch>`, `git clean` or rebase. Cursor never pushes: it commits locally only, and Claude pushes.
7. VPS: read-only for Cursor. Deploys and VPS changes are done only by Claude; request them in section 11.
8. Runtime: only one Windows agent worker may run (K-53 COORD-3). `scripts/agent_ctl.py` replaces the manual `RUNTIME LOCK` line in `plan.md` section 2.6: check the worker with `.venv_312\Scripts\python.exe scripts\agent_ctl.py status` and start, stop or restart it only with `.venv_312\Scripts\python.exe scripts\agent_ctl.py start|stop|restart --by cursor --reason '<TASK-ID>'` (`wait` and `logs` only read). Never start it another way (`python -m src.core.agent`, `start-agent.bat`, `dev.bat`, Electron with `JARVIS_LOCAL_BACKEND=1`), never kill python processes, and append the `done_highlight.md` entry that `agent_ctl` prints. The UI dev server (5173) and preview (4173) ports are yours and need no lock line.
9. The GitHub repo is public: never print, paste or commit secrets from `.env` files, and keep secrets, passwords, keys, voice samples, logs, chat data and details of non-JARVIS apps or servers out of tracked files (code, docs, `plan.md`, `done_highlight.md`) and commit messages.
10. Contracts: read `docs/CONTRACTS.md` before touching any API, socket event, LiveKit topic, env name or schema. A change is requested as `REQ-CONTRACT <contract> <proposal>` in `plan.md` section 11; only Claude edits `docs/CONTRACTS.md`.
